## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design for multi-tenant Azure AI apps with data residency, cost controls, and human-in-the-loop guardrails. It emphasizes end-to-end data flow, governance, and observability in real production settings.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Deployment patterns across regions
- API Management and Front Door for routing and auth
- Grounding using a versioned KB in Blob + Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics and policy checks
- Per-tenant budgets with Cosmos DB-backed state and escalation queues
- Data Lake auditing and rollback strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
async function maybeCallOpenAI(tenantId, tokensNext){
  const budget = await getBudget(tenantId);
  if(budget - tokensNext < 0) {
    await enqueueHumanReview(tenantId);
    throw new Error("Budget exceeded");
  }
  return callOpenAI(/* ... */);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant data residency across regions?
- What testing strategy ensures budget gating and humane escalation stays responsive?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical multi-tenant localization, content grounding, and integration of Azure services with OpenAI.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and translation using Azure Text Analytics and Azure Translator
- Grounding OpenAI responses to a KB stored in Azure Blob and indexed by Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant locale settings for currency/date formatting
- Error handling and fallback
- APIM as gateway and request routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch for data flow
async function handleQuery(input, tenant){
  const lang = detectLang(input);
  const q = translate(input, 'en');
  const grounded = await queryOpenAI(q, tenant);
  const res = translate(grounded, lang, lang);
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test locale formatting across locales?
- How would you handle translation latency and partial failures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests hands-on ability to weave Azure AI, policy governance, and regulatory constraints into a live assistant that scales per tenant and remains auditable.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI behind API Management
- Grounding with Cognitive Search over versioned KB in Blob
- Per-tenant policy gating via Key Vault keys
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- Audit logs in Data Lake
- Fallback to sanitized checklist on gate/confidence failure

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: gate checks before OpenAI call
function shouldFallback(prompt, budget, policy) {
  if (policy.violationDetected) return true;
  if (estimateCost(prompt) > budget) return true;
  if (promptContainsPII(prompt)) return true;
  return false;
}
```

